  <fragment slot="dream log">
    A discotheque of sinister strangers with faces in flux, contorting in and
    out of familiarity. Nausea and the taste of metal. The room is big and then
    it’s small until it’s big again. No one knows me here. They are dancing
    automatons. If I’m the intruder why do I feel like prey? There is something
    beautiful in the danger, glowing and radioactive. I soon find out why the
    automatons dance. Whatever compels them takes me in as well, but only
    somatically. Whatever remains of my self is small and petrified within my
    body. The center of the dance floor collapses into a void and we succumb to
    the whirlpool. Lasers bend, ambient haze condenses into small vortexes, the
    bassline constricts my throat. A LAPSE I am left with an eerie sense of
    having been somewhere else, and a metallic echo in my mouth.
  </fragment>

  <fragment slot="bio">
    Sofiya V is a multidisciplinary artist and designer based in New York City.
  </fragment>
